{
  "example": "Given a requirement `foo.ready` and a named example `foo.case`, `habeas info 'foo.*'` displays both, and `habeas status 'foo.*' --all` lists both with their kinds and evidence states. {cite}`requirements.cli.info` {cite}`requirements.cli.status`",
  "determination": false,
  "rationale": "The `info` half of the example is covered. The `status` half is not covered by any test that matches the scenario.\n\n**Covered: `habeas info '<glob>'` shows a requirement and an example.**\n- `info_renders_exact_and_glob_matches_as_markdown_without_an_index` (tests/commands.rs, around lines 460–520) runs `info requirements.*`.\n- It asserts that requirements and the example `requirements.case` are all rendered. The example appears with its `## Example` section, and the matches are in name order and separated by `---`.\n- This matches \"`habeas info 'foo.*'` displays both\".\n\n**Not covered: `habeas status '<glob>' --all` lists a requirement and an example together with kinds and evidence states.** The `status` assertions that touch a glob are split across tests:\n- `status_and_info_accept_a_definition_selection` (around lines 701–730) runs `status requirements.c* --all`.\n  - It checks only that the example row `| \\`requirements.case\\` (example)` appears and that `requirements.ready` is absent.\n  - The glob matches only the example, so no requirement is listed in the same output.\n  - It makes no assertion about the evidence state of the matched row.\n- `commands_report_invalid_arguments_and_unmatched_selectors` (around lines 527–570) runs `status requirements.*ready --all`.\n  - It checks `(requirement)` kind labels for two requirements.\n  - It matches no example and asserts no evidence state.\n- `status_lists_nonvalid_requirements_and_all_option_in_name_order` (around lines 366–420) checks evidence states such as `Valid`, and the `(example)` label, only for unfiltered `status` and `status --all`. It uses no glob.\n\nNo test runs `status` with a glob that matches both a requirement and a named example. No test asserts evidence states for rows selected by a glob. The scenario's status expectation, \"lists both with their kinds and evidence states\", is therefore only inferred from separate partial checks. No FIXME acknowledges this gap.\n\nA test like `status 'requirements.*' --all` that asserts a requirement row, an example row, and their states would close it.",
